35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,Two admins retire this year. The last posting stayed open for eleven months.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The yard scanners are a mix of old models. The 2021 trial was ringed with spreadsheets.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"Capital requests are trimmed, but operating lines pass easily. Renewals for add-ons climb yearly.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,Support was scattered across four suppliers. The outage sat unowned for two days.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,We skipped three upgrade windows because testing took weeks. The 2018 data lift had errors for a year.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, if operating lines are the trap, we can't afford a system that needs constant add-ons.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Yumi, unowned support is terrifying. We need a vendor who actually answers when things break.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Misaki, I agree. The board ignores the recurring costs. We must avoid modular traps.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Kenji, I agree. A regional team might be better than scattered suppliers.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the upgrade history shows we can't handle big, complex changes. We need something stable.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Misaki,,The supervisors dropped the new routines within weeks. We need a system that fits their habits.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Kenji,,The depot calendar has no freeze window in winter. Any cutover then is a disaster.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Toshio,,The bundled agreements held their price. The separately licensed pieces climbed.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Yumi,,The warehouse rules were rewritten twice mid-year. The scope never survived a full year.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The dispatch tool has been on our racks since 2012. It's aging in place.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Misaki,,"We need a vendor who understands our people, not just our software.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Kenji,,We need a system that works with our old yard devices and our crazy calendar.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Toshio,,We need a fixed price. No hidden add-ons. No climbing renewal costs.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Yumi,,"We need clear ownership. One team, one point of contact.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,"We need a system that doesn't require constant, risky upgrades.","{""words"":10,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
