60,3,1,talk,Misaki,,Candidate D has an engineering team present. That helps with the admin gap.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Kenji,,Candidate D is built for transport. It might handle our yard devices better.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Candidate B is a hosted suite with fixed configuration. That sounds like a fixed price.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Yumi,,Candidate B has a regional service team. That solves the ownership problem.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate D is on our own servers. That means we control the upgrades.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Toshio, but D is on our servers. If the admins leave, who maintains it?","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Yumi, B is hosted. But does it work with our old yard scanners?","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Misaki, D's engineering team is present through rollout. That might bridge the gap.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Yumi,,"@Kenji, B's regional team should handle the integration. We need to trust them.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, D's on-premise nature means we can upgrade when we're ready, not when the vendor forces it.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Misaki,,I worry about D's long-term maintenance if our admins leave. But the rollout support is key.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Kenji,,I'm leaning towards D. It's built for us. The yard compatibility is a big plus.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Toshio,,B's fixed configuration appeals to me. No hidden add-ons. But I fear the hosting costs.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Yumi,,B's clear ownership is what I need. I can't risk another unowned outage.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"D's stability is what I want. No risky, complex upgrades. Just a solid, transport-specific tool.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Misaki,,I vote for D. The rollout support is critical for our staffing issues.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Kenji,,I vote for D. It fits our yard and our calendar.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I vote for B. The fixed price is too important to ignore.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Yumi,,I vote for B. The regional team gives me peace of mind.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,I vote for D. It avoids the upgrade traps I've seen.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
